Let $0 \le n \le 719$. Divide successively:

- $n = 120e + r_1$, $0 \le r_1 < 120$;
- $r_1 = 24d + r_2$, $0 \le r_2 < 24$;
- $r_2 = 6c + r_3$, $0 \le r_3 < 6$;
- $r_3 = 2b + r_4$, $0 \le r_4 < 2$;
- $r_4 = 1 \cdot a$.

Then $n = e(5!) + d(4!) + c(3!) + b(2!) + a(1!)$ with all quotients non-negative integers. The bounds hold:

- $120e \le n < 720$, so $e \le 5$;
- $24d \le r_1 < 120$, so $d \le 4$;
- $6c \le r_2 < 24$, so $c \le 3$;
- $2b \le r_3 < 6$, so $b \le 2$;
- $a = r_4 < 2$, so $a \le 1$.

So every $n$ with $0 \le n \le N$ can be written in the required form. ∎
